1. Foundations (global setup)

CSS variables (:root): your color palette, fonts, spacing sizes, and border radius, defined once and reused everywhere. 
This is the heart of your brand guidelines.
Reset / box-sizing: * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; } so sizing behaves predictably.
html and body: base font, font size, line height, background color, text color.

2. Typography

Headings (h1 to h6): font, size scale, weight, color, spacing
Paragraphs (p): line height, max width for readability
Links (a): normal, :hover, :focus, :visited states
Lists (ul, ol, li): bullets, spacing, indentation
Text details: strong, em, blockquote, small

3. Page structure (layout)

header: logo/title area
nav: menu links, active page highlight, hover effects
main: content wrapper with max-width and centering
section / article: spacing between content blocks
footer: copyright, links, contact info
Container class: a reusable centered wrapper (e.g. .container)
Grid / Flexbox: for arranging columns, rows, and card layouts

4. Components (reusable pieces)

Buttons (button, .btn): default, hover, active, disabled
Cards (.card): background, padding, shadow, border radius. Perfect for team member profiles on an about page
Images (img): max-width: 100%, rounded corners, object-fit for profile photos
Forms (input, textarea, label, select): if you have a contact form
Tables (table, th, td): only if needed
Hero / banner section: big intro area at the top of the page

5. Responsiveness

Media queries (@media): adjusting layout for tablet and mobile (e.g. stacking columns, collapsing the nav)
Viewport meta tag (in the HTML, not CSS, but required for this to work)

6. Brand guideline extras

Utility classes: .text-center, .bg-primary, .text-accent, etc.
Spacing scale: consistent values like 8px, 16px, 24px, 32px
Accessibility: visible :focus outlines and enough color contrast between text and background